---
title: Sign a PDF with a .p12 / .pfx certificate
description: Apply a PKCS#7 digital signature using your own certificate — private, in-browser.
relatedTool: digital-sign-pdf
---

Create a **cryptographic digital signature** — not just visible text — using your certificate file.

## Steps

1. Open **Digital Sign PDF**.
2. Upload the PDF to sign.
3. Upload your `.p12` or `.pfx` certificate.
4. Enter the certificate password (used locally only).
5. Download the signed PDF.

## Tips

> **vs. Sign PDF:** **Sign PDF** adds a visible signature image or text. **Digital Sign PDF** embeds a PKCS#7 signature verifiable in Adobe Acrobat.

- Adobe verifies signature structure; trust depends on your certificate authority.
- Keep certificate files secure — they never leave your browser during signing.

